{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes","id":1455849,"title":"A Technique Equivalent For Mega-Attributes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-31T06:47:05-07:00","id":1455849,"title":"A Technique Equivalent For Mega-Attributes","content":"So, on a thematic level, Mega-Attributes are one of the things that really separates Aberrant from other supers games. Sure, being superhuman is a common theme, but it being separate from powers and quite as all-encompassing as Mega-Attributes is fairly unique, and the way that NPC Mega-Attributes were handled in 1E (ie: it was a rare Nova that wasn't shown with several), created a very specific and unique dynamic. 'Dark Stars' with low ratings in all the Mega-attributes were and are also fairly unique and interesting conceptually.<br /> <br /> On a mechanical level in 2E, however, there are some cost issues with implementing this dynamic. Specifically, Powers are actually much cheaper than Mega-Attributes (due to how Technique works), and some can even grant Mega-Attributes...and thus the best way to build, say, a Brick is the Transformation power, not actually buying Mega-Attributes, while the best way to 'have 1 dot of every Mega-Attribute' is actually Boost and Variable or Extra Attribute. That's counterintuitive for new players and not super fun, IMO.<br /> <br /> In fact, I can build a Nova with Quantum 4, Boost 4 (All Attributes, Subtle, Maintained, Ramp Up -3...activated when you wake up in the morning and left on all day) and, as a Technique, Transformation 5 (Maintained, Subtle, Extra Attributes 3) or thereabouts who walks around with straight 5s in all Attributes, and at least two dots in every single Mega-Attribute (and 5 in all the physical ones, plus Toughness 5), as a starting character. That's exploitive and should generally be vetoed by the SG, but a biokinetic, say, with Boost (Might, Dex, and Stm) and a Technique for Transformation (as well as others for Quantum Attack and Healing), on the other hand, is a pretty reasonable concept and runs into the same problem of 'better at Mega-Attributes than people who actually bought Mega-Attributes'. Which is a problem.<br /> <br /> So, I've added the following Mega-Edge to my games as a House Rule:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Polymath (O \u2013 OOOOO):</u></b><br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Quantum equal to dots, one Mega-Attribute at 2+<br /> <br /> Select one Mega-Attribute. For every dot in this Edge receive additional dots in Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges equal to that Mega-Attribute's rating. These points may not be used to purchase the Technique or Q-Tech Mega-Edges or to increase any Mega-Attribute or Mega-Edge above the rating of the original Mega-Attribute. A character may only ever have this Edge once, though if another Mega-Attribute ever equals their rating in the Mega-Attribute it effects, they may switch it to be based on that Mega-Attribute instead. Since this Mega-Edge has no mechanical effect beyond changing costs, it should not generally be listed on NPCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Technically, the above mentioned Boost/Transformation combo remains more cost effective than this, but this lets you actually take advantage of Mega-Edges and the difference is a lot less glaring, and many more concepts can and should have access to it (the Boost/Transformation combo does also have real downsides while Polymath just doesn't). It does necessitate one high Mega-Attribute even on a thematically 'Dark Star' Nova, but both Cunning and Composure (especially Composure) actually work well for that as 'subtle' Mega-Attributes. I highly recommend something like this for any game wanting to focus on Mega-Attributes, especially those with relatively new players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T07:05:48-07:00","id":1455850,"title":"","content":"I use a similar idea, but just giving more options to Technique Mega Edge (but making one for it is a better option).<br /> <br /> In my idea you add the technique to a Mega Attribute and gain the MAtt rank times the technique mega edge dots as dots of Mega Edges related to that MAtt (Technique is not a valid one).<br /> <br /> So if you get Technique to Mega Might, you can get Mega Lifting, Mega Crush, etc, but not any Mega Cunning mega edge for example, or any dot in Mega Dexterity.<br /> <br /> A bit less versatile than yours, but I honestly prefer that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T07:40:58-07:00","id":1455852,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think that the problem is that Technique is too powerful: you get a whole other power for the cost of just one dot in a Mega-Edge, and the only downside is that if you want both active at once, you need to split the activation dice pool. That feels more like it should be handled by requiring every power separately, then applying a negative tag to each power in a suite to represent the shared activation dice pool: say, -1 to each if two powers are in the suite, -2 to each if three powers are in the suite, and so on. (This escalating discount is based on the idea that the more powers you try to activate, the thinner you have to spread your successes.)<br /> <br /> The Technique approach is only priced reasonably if the powers in the suite cannot be active at the same time: you'd basically be buying one power, and supplementing it with the ability to swap it out for something else as needed. So you pay the full price for one power, plus one Mega-Edge dot for each alternative way to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T09:15:09-07:00","id":1455855,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think it\u2019s the one thing that allows Novas to follow other splats in the XP cost benefit.<br /> <br /> At first a Nova gains a bunch of extra,XP, but everything a nova can buy is really expensive. You may think it\u2019s about making it tempting to buy it corrupted, but at the long run (when you already got all the transformations you want and are already afraid of transcendence), any modification in the powers costs a lot of XP.<br /> <br /> For example, Psion/Psiad powers costs 6-8 so per dot, but you gain an improvement on the previous levels (as per dot table) and an entire new power (at least on a cheaper way to use it), while a Nova would need to spend 1 \u201cNova Dot\u201d in the range, 1 duration tag, and another in the new effect, also, the nova dot costs twice the cost of the Psion equivalent, in other words, 6 times more to get the same effect.<br /> <br /> In other words, Novas start powerful, but after 150 more XP, the Psion will have 15+ New mode dots (considering they spend some in psi and other stuff), while a nova will have spent most of the same XP in just 5 or 6 tags and a 3 or 4 ranks in powers (and maybe +1 or 2 quantum), and the 15+ dots in modes will grant lots of advantages beside the powers themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T09:21:28-07:00","id":1455856,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455850#post1455850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use a similar idea, but just giving more options to Technique Mega Edge (but making one for it is a better option).</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455850#post1455850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In my idea you add the technique to a Mega Attribute and gain the MAtt rank times the technique mega edge dots as dots of Mega Edges related to that MAtt (Technique is not a valid one).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So if you get Technique to Mega Might, you can get Mega Lifting, Mega Crush, etc, but not any Mega Cunning mega edge for example, or any dot in Mega Dexterity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A bit less versatile than yours, but I honestly prefer that way.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This strongly encourages heavy specialization (which is potentially a feature rather than a bug, I admit, though I prefer diversification), but also reduces the utility of saving points like this. I mean, there are enough Mega-Might Edges to make this worth buying maybe once, ditto for Mega-Stamina and most other Mega-Attributes (Dexterity, Intellect, and Cunning are exceptions, but even there in many cases we're talking only two or three at most...any Power can easily have five), which is effectively saying 'You can buy Technique on Mega-attributes, but only once per Attribute'. That's certainly better than not being able to do so at all, points-wise, but doesn't really close the gap in the way I'm trying to.<br /> <br /> It certainly doesn't help make the 'Dark Star' Nova with low ratings in every Mega-Attribute more affordable and effective, and making that more affordable and effective is definitely one of the goals of this House Rule.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455852#post1455852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think that the problem is that Technique is too powerful: you get a whole other power for the cost of just one dot in a Mega-Edge, and the only downside is that if you want both active at once, you need to split the activation dice pool. That feels more like it should be handled by requiring every power separately, then applying a negative tag to each power in a suite to represent the shared activation dice pool: say, -1 to each if two powers are in the suite, -2 to each if three powers are in the suite, and so on. (This escalating discount is based on the idea that the more powers you try to activate, the thinner you have to spread your successes.)<br /> <br /> The Technique approach is only priced reasonably if the powers in the suite cannot be active at the same time: you'd basically be buying one power, and supplementing it with the ability to swap it out for something else as needed. So you pay the full price for one power, plus one Mega-Edge dot for each alternative way to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technique is an amazing must-have on a mechanical level, and reducing its power level or removing it entirely is a reasonable House Rule in its own right if you want to decrease Nova power level...but doing so doesn't actually solve the disparity I'm aiming to fix. Even with Technique nonexistent, either the Boost or Transform powers I listed on their own create a huge and unwarranted disparity between Powers and Mega-attributes.<br /> <br /> I mean, Boost 4 (All Attributes) results in straight 5s in the mundane attributes and, on a starting character, a total of 16 dots of Mega-Attributes all on its own. That should not be <i>by far</i> the best way to have low levels in every Mega-Attribute, and yet it is, and no Technique is required to make it so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","user":"Deadmanwalking","date":". 07-31-2021, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T09:35:38-07:00","id":1455858,"title":"","content":"1) Wouldn't just making Mega-Attributes much cheaper in XP be a better solution? Why/Why not do this instead? \ud83e\udd14<br /> 2) If so, what would be the best XP cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T09:37:52-07:00","id":1455859,"title":"","content":"Boost 4 (All attributes) has a quite good cost, I mean, it costs 4 (from the ranks) + 8 (from the additional attributes) and require Q4, also it consumes 18 quantum to activate (variable attribute reduce the cost because allow you to boost only what you want) every 4 rounds, it will drain quite fast the character quantum pool. But yes, it grants a bunch of dice and a good amount of Mega Attributes to be used in emergencies.<br /> <br /> I personally would embrace Transformation as the cheaper all flexible Darkstar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T09:42:06-07:00","id":1455860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455858#post1455858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Wouldn't just making Mega-Attributes much cheaper in XP be a better solution? Why/Why not do this instead? \ud83e\udd14<br /> 2) If so, what would be the best XP cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) No, it actually unbalance the lower end scale of the char evolution. Techniques make powers exponentially cheaper the higher the Quantum, but change almost nothing to low quantum characters. If you reduce the cost of Mega Attributes you make them cheaper all the way along, it will give a advantage to low quantum characters to be Mega-human while it would still be less cost effective in the Q5+ end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T09:54:24-07:00","id":1455861,"title":"","content":"Deadmanwalking, what do you think about this?<br /> <br /> Couldn't 8XP work?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455858#post1455858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Wouldn't just making Mega-Attributes much cheaper in XP be a better solution? Why/Why not do this instead? \ud83e\udd14<br /> 2) If so, what would be the best XP cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>3) Mateus, I thought that making Dark Stars feasible was the whole point of the House Rule... The goal is to make beginner Dark Stars feasible, right? It doesn't mean high Quantum Novas should have all Mega-Attributes (or most) at a high rating, just that they'll keep a lot of low level ones if they started as Dark Stars. Also, we should remember that Mega-Attb ratings cant be higher than Quantum, and that the biggest advantages come from Mega-Edges right? (that would still be 12XP). Only Mega-Attb would cost 8 XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","user":"Timecrafter","date":". 07-31-2021, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T10:57:34-07:00","id":1455862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455858#post1455858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Wouldn't just making Mega-Attributes much cheaper in XP be a better solution? Why/Why not do this instead? \ud83e\udd14<br /> 2) If so, what would be the best XP cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>Better in what sense? It'd be simpler, but I don't know about better.<br /> <br /> Polymath has the advantage of being fairly symmetrical with Technique while lower XP costs...don't, and run into a few other bits of weirdness as well. Assuming 8 XP, at Quantum 5, you can get 15 dots of Mgea-Attributes for the same cost as 30 dots of Powers...which is not a huge improvement over the status quo, frankly (I mean, it's slightly better than the current 10, but still way short). On the other hand at any less than 8 xp you're rapidly running into them being too good for what they cost (indeed, that's debatably true even at 8 xp). Polymath hard caps how many you can get with a cost break, which is good, and requires you to invest in Quantum for the cost break to kick in, which I like for a variety of reasons (consistency, Quantum being a good measure of raw power for everyone, have to invest in Quantum even if you don't have things that cost it to use, etc.).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455859#post1455859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boost 4 (All attributes) has a quite good cost, I mean, it costs 4 (from the ranks) + 8 (from the additional attributes) and require Q4, also it consumes 18 quantum to activate (variable attribute reduce the cost because allow you to boost only what you want) every 4 rounds, it will drain quite fast the character quantum pool. But yes, it grants a bunch of dice and a good amount of Mega Attributes to be used in emergencies.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455859#post1455859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I personally would embrace Transformation as the cheaper all flexible Darkstar.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The trick with Boost is you make it Maintained, activate it when you wake up, and then just have it on all the time for all practical purposes. Sure, it's pricey, but if it's your only power who cares? Not like you were using that Quantum for anything else.<br /> <br /> Transformation can't get you Mental or Social Mega-Attributes, which is why Boost is preferred for this 'build' (though, as I said, the 'ideal' version just has both, one as a Technique of the other). </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455861#post1455861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deadmanwalking, what do you think about this?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455861#post1455861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Couldn't 8XP work?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Not very well IMO, see above.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mateus, I thought that making Dark Stars feasible was the whole point of the House Rule... The goal is to make beginner Dark Stars feasible, right? It doesn't mean high Quantum Novas should have all Mega-Attributes (or most) at a high rating, just that they'll keep a lot of low level ones if they started as Dark Stars. Also, we should remember that Mega-Attb ratings cant be higher than Quantum, and that the biggest advantages come from Mega-Edges right? (that would still be 12XP). Only Mega-Attb would cost 8 XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the only goal. It's also to make 'I want to create a Brick, I'm gonna grab maxed out Mega-Might, Mega-Stamina, and Toughness' a reasonable choice, along with other similar 'I'm good at Mega-Attributes' concepts. At the moment such Mega-Attribute heavy concepts are penalized as compared to Power heavy ones. I want to fix that. 'Dark Stars' are one example of such a concept, but not the only one, or the only one I want to effect.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T10:59:07-07:00","id":1455863,"title":"","content":"While I think making Darkstars feasible is one of the advantages, I don\u2019t think the idea of a Techinique applied to Mega Attributes dark star thing, for 2 reasons:<br /> The idea requires Rank 2 MAtt, what is not really \u201cDark Star\u201d as it is quite noticeable as very superhuman (like throwing trucks and being almost completely bulletproof)<br /> Also, technique gains weight after Q3+ when you can have 3+ extra powers with a lot of ranks.<br /> <br /> So, reducing the cost would make Darkstars more versatile, but at the long shot it would not add much to the cost/benefit of buying Mega Attributes, you would just have a few more dots (reducing from 12 to 8 would allow you to buy one more for every 2 you have, but the max rank would be limited to the same level, as you said) but in the long run powers and techniques would be far cheaper (Q5 with 5 techniques reduce the average dot cost of a power by a factor of 5+ according to the number of tags you have in the powers, so every dot will cost about 2,5xp or so)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T11:03:10-07:00","id":1455864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455863#post1455863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I think making Darkstars feasible is one of the advantages, I don\u2019t think the idea of a Techinique applied to Mega Attributes dark star thing, for 2 reasons:<br /> The idea requires Rank 2 MAtt, what is not really \u201cDark Star\u201d as it is quite noticeable as very superhuman (like throwing trucks and being almost completely bulletproof)<br /> Also, technique gains weight after Q3+ when you can have 3+ extra powers with a lot of ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Dark Stars built with Polymath, I'd just make their 'high stat' Mega-Cunning or Mega-Composure. Both are actually quite subtle in terms of what they do most of the time, especially Mega-Composure with Subtle Presence. Most of their other Mega-Attributes stay at 1 (maybe 2 for things like Mega-Intellect, Mega-Manipulation, or Mega-Resolve). Works pretty well, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T11:18:28-07:00","id":1455866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455864#post1455864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For Dark Stars built with Polymath, I'd just make their 'high stat' Mega-Cunning or Mega-Composure. Both are actually quite subtle in terms of what they do most of the time, especially Mega-Composure with Subtle Presence. Most of their other Mega-Attributes stay at 1 (maybe 2 for things like Mega-Intellect, Mega-Manipulation, or Mega-Resolve). Works pretty well, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, you can have a guy like Luke Cage that is completely human and Mega Though and Strong. The problems is I see the Dark Star concept as a Q1 Nova with no overt powers. So, it\u2019s not just visually human, but to a quantum detector it\u2019s possible that the power level is so low it won\u2019t recognize as a quantum user. That\u2019s my personal view, and the one I was using, sorry if I misinterpreted it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T11:35:09-07:00","id":1455868,"title":"","content":"My own vision of a Dark Star is someone that can pass for an exceptional human even when using their full abilities, not necessarily a specific Quantum rating (so Luke Cage would, IMO, not count as he's overtly superhumanly tough and strong...but someone with Mega-Composure 5 could totally count, at least in theory, because they can pass as human even when using that Mega-Attribute to its fullest). I <i>think</i> only Dormancy actually gets you past Quantum detector even at Q1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T12:18:40-07:00","id":1455869,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that even a single dot of, say, Mega-Might, when used to its fullest, displays obviously superhuman levels of ability. In that case, it's not so much a matter of the Nova being able to lift something that a mere mortal could not, as it is that he can do with e something that even the strongest baseline would struggle with.<br /> <br /> But yeah, so called dark stars aren't defined by any in-game hard and fast rule such as no mega attribute over two; they are defined by their subtlety. They are the ones who are technically superhuman, but don't seem to be. Which, as a rule of thumb, does indeed mean low mega attributes, limited mega edges, and no quantum powers.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I don't consider Dark Stars to be all that interesting: their narrative role has largely been usurped by Talents. In the original game, they were the only option that you had to make someone who was extraordinary but not obviously superhuman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-31-2021, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T15:55:43-07:00","id":1455881,"title":"","content":"One thing I think changed from 1e to TC is that some of what would be Novas by 1e standard become Talents and Psiads instead, and it\u2019s basically stated that way.<br /> <br /> Some of the most covert powers become Gifts and mere use of Inspiration (Luck and Intuition come to mind) and others are Psiad material (Mental Blast, Precognition, Telepathy, etc). Sure you can say Novas can gain those powers and use as Mental or Social Mega Edges, but it can be played as Talents and Psiads could be called Darkstar Novas as people don\u2019t understand how their powers work (and in fact a quantum detector would not even detect them).<br /> <br /> We even have some characters described in different ways (Sophia Rousseau was a Nova and is now a Psiad, and Maggie Mercer was a particularly capable baseline in Aberrant d20 and now is a Psiad too). Even in the antagonists we have a Psiad as example, and she believes she is a Nova, even part of Teragen. I would say a meaningful part of the Novas in the world are in fact overt Talents and Psiads that really think they are Novas with some limited powers that work different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T16:58:10-07:00","id":1455886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455869#post1455869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the opinion that even a single dot of, say, Mega-Might, when used to its fullest, displays obviously superhuman levels of ability. In that case, it's not so much a matter of the Nova being able to lift something that a mere mortal could not, as it is that he can do with e something that even the strongest baseline would struggle with.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The game itself seems to disagree, with Scale 2 strength listed as 'Strong-man'. That's impressive, but not overtly impossible. The same is true of most Scale 2 stuff that's actually increased by Mega-Attributes (Speed and Durability are more overtly inhuman at Scale 2...but Mega-Attributes don't directly raise those). </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455869#post1455869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, so called dark stars aren't defined by any in-game hard and fast rule such as no mega attribute over two; they are defined by their subtlety. They are the ones who are technically superhuman, but don't seem to be. Which, as a rule of thumb, does indeed mean low mega attributes, limited mega edges, and no quantum powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, that's my usual definition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455869#post1455869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I don't consider Dark Stars to be all that interesting: their narrative role has largely been usurped by Talents. In the original game, they were the only option that you had to make someone who was extraordinary but not obviously superhuman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Personally, I think there's a distinct difference inasmuch as Talents tend to be very good within a specific area, while a Dark Star is more likely to be omnicompetent, being pretty good at <i>literally everything</i>. That's a pretty big difference. But regardless, as I said, this House Rule (while intended to be helpful to those who want to play a Dark Star) is hardly exclusive to such characters. It's also intended to make more overt Mega-Attribute users easier and more reasonable to create.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455881#post1455881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I think changed from 1e to TC is that some of what would be Novas by 1e standard become Talents and Psiads instead, and it\u2019s basically stated that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is certainly true, but it's by no means all of them, or even all of the subtle ones.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455881#post1455881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the most covert powers become Gifts and mere use of Inspiration (Luck and Intuition come to mind) and others are Psiad material (Mental Blast, Precognition, Telepathy, etc). Sure you can say Novas can gain those powers and use as Mental or Social Mega Edges, but it can be played as Talents and Psiads could be called Darkstar Novas as people don\u2019t understand how their powers work (and in fact a quantum detector would not even detect them).</div> </div> </div> </div>Psiads certainly (though some 'psychics' definitely remain Novas, Andre Corbin being a sterling example, but Psyche of T2M likely being another one and others certainly possible), but Talents seem to me to be generally just considered impressive baselines. That's certainly the tack they've gone with on NPCs who are Talents (all of whom, I believe, were baselines in 1E). Luck and Intuition can also be duplicated by Novas via the Foresight Mega-Edge (used subconsciously) and some decent Mega-Cunning, something I'd expect high Luck Novas like Ricardo Montoya-Bernal and the like to definitely do this edition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455881#post1455881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We even have some characters described in different ways (Sophia Rousseau was a Nova and is now a Psiad, and Maggie Mercer was a particularly capable baseline in Aberrant d20 and now is a Psiad too). Even in the antagonists we have a Psiad as example, and she believes she is a Nova, even part of Teragen. I would say a meaningful part of the Novas in the world are in fact overt Talents and Psiads that really think they are Novas with some limited powers that work different.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> Totally fair as far as it goes, but Psiads while 'weak' in Nova terms are actually usually pretty overt in having actual powers...not in the sense of not being able to hide them, but in the sense of the things they do not having a rational explanation other than 'superpowers', which is a bit different. Talents, meanwhile, as I state above, come off more as very competent baselines than any kind of Nova, even to themselves. I have a hard time seeing a Talent ever mistaking themselves for a Nova like Psiads might, while a real Dark Star with Mega-Attributes in everything will probably realize what they are most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T17:30:32-07:00","id":1455888,"title":"","content":"The point in Scale 2 Strong Man is that he do do it with a huge effort and for just some time, while a Mega Might 1 can do the same all day long with no restriction. In game terms the Strong man has a skill trick to gain scale for a single action, while Mega Might consumes nothing from the Nova, basically the first can maybe lift a car long enough to save a person under it, while a Nova can hold the car up as if it was a person or a travel bag, may get the Nova tired, but it will take some time.<br /> <br /> While I agree most Talents would be considered baselines in all ways, some of them may gain a more conscious use of lucky, and while not capable of do specific things, are always in the good side of the scale. Talking about scale, they can literally take a punch of a mega strong guy and end up with no more than a black eye. Take Batman for example, he is baseline in all ways possible, yet some people stat him as a Darkstar because he is\u2026 well, he is Batman, he is always prepared, have all the right tools and plans, to the point seams he can read the script prior the game\u2026 basically dramatic editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-31-2021, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T18:27:56-07:00","id":1455893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455888#post1455888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point in Scale 2 Strong Man is that he do do it with a huge effort and for just some time, while a Mega Might 1 can do the same all day long with no restriction. In game terms the Strong man has a skill trick to gain scale for a single action, while Mega Might consumes nothing from the Nova, basically the first can maybe lift a car long enough to save a person under it, while a Nova can hold the car up as if it was a person or a travel bag, may get the Nova tired, but it will take some time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Someone with a single dot in a mega attribute can do with ease what the best of the best among baseline struggle with. And the second dot let the Nova do things with ease that novas with only one dot struggle with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T00:50:03-07:00","id":1455908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455888#post1455888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point in Scale 2 Strong Man is that he do do it with a huge effort and for just some time, while a Mega Might 1 can do the same all day long with no restriction. In game terms the Strong man has a skill trick to gain scale for a single action, while Mega Might consumes nothing from the Nova, basically the first can maybe lift a car long enough to save a person under it, while a Nova can hold the car up as if it was a person or a travel bag, may get the Nova tired, but it will take some time.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I'm not sure I agree. A Nova with, say, Might 2, Athletics 0, and Mega-Might 1 is, IMO, well within the realm of human capability. Sure, they have Scale, but a human can try things at higher than their normal scale at a 'mere' +2 Difficulty. The Might 5, Athletics 5 guy is frankly more likely to succeed at a Difficulty 3 roll than the Nova is at Difficulty 1. The Nova definitely knows he's gotten stronger than he was pre-Eruption, but outside observers can't tell he's a Nova from strength alone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455888#post1455888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree most Talents would be considered baselines in all ways, some of them may gain a more conscious use of lucky, and while not capable of do specific things, are always in the good side of the scale. Talking about scale, they can literally take a punch of a mega strong guy and end up with no more than a black eye. Take Batman for example, he is baseline in all ways possible, yet some people stat him as a Darkstar because he is\u2026 well, he is Batman, he is always prepared, have all the right tools and plans, to the point seams he can read the script prior the game\u2026 basically dramatic editing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talents who actually have The Bigger They Are and encounter Nova opposition are a bit of an exception because yeah, those folks definitely know they're something special, but that's a small subcategory of Talents taken as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455893#post1455893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Exactly. Someone with a single dot in a mega attribute can do with ease what the best of the best among baseline struggle with. And the second dot let the Nova do things with ease that novas with only one dot struggle with.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I agree on the second dot. At that point you're just exceeding human capability on a regular basis (though some, like Manipulation or Intelligence, may be able to act like they aren't). But one level and a mediocre normal Attribute? You're impressive, but not necessarily superhuman. I mean, a 4+ and a Mega-Attribute is definitely superhuman, but a 2 and Mega Attribute 1? Not so much.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But really, this is a bit off topic. The House Rule I propose does nothing in any way to change how recognizable low level Mega-Attributes are, just how expensive they are to get. So, much as the topic is of interest to me as well, we should probably drop it and focus on the Polymath/Technique/Costs of Stats discussion.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T01:23:12-07:00","id":1455910,"title":"","content":"The cost apart, another aspect that needs to be covered is that some of the powers many characters in comics have are covered by Mega Edges, and so they don\u2019t get covered by techniques ar all, cyberkinesis, super speed, telepathy, etc.<br /> <br /> Your approach to the rules open this side of the rules in a way my approach don\u2019t, as you can combine super speed and shockwave to make a sonic boom, instead of 2 independent powers, but it keep powers out of the way, so a quantum attack (punch of infinite mass) and a sonic boom must be independent (bad example, because you can make sonic boom with quantum attack, but you got the idea, technique with power and mega stuff combined).<br /> <br /> Another option is you can create techniques out of mega edges, instead of powers only, combining everything as you pleased. The issue there is that most of the techniques don\u2019t evolve as powers do, they just have a fixed cost and that\u2019s it (they can get tags, but it\u2019s not that many that fit) while powers can gain extra dots and tags.<br /> <br /> I am just pointing things, not bringing solutions\u2026 maybe later I can bring something solid to discuss\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T03:56:10-07:00","id":1455918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455908#post1455908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I agree. A Nova with, say, Might 2, Athletics 0, and Mega-Might 1 is, IMO, well within the realm of human capability. Sure, they have Scale, but a human can try things at higher than their normal scale at a 'mere' +2 Difficulty. The Might 5, Athletics 5 guy is frankly more likely to succeed at a Difficulty 3 roll than the Nova is at Difficulty 1. The Nova definitely knows he's gotten stronger than he was pre-Eruption, but outside observers can't tell he's a Nova from strength alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a quick nitpick, and then I'll drop it: the Might 5/Athletics 5 guy will look like a bodybuilder (because, frankly, he <i>is</i> a body builder); the Might 2/Athletics 0/Mega-Might 1 guy probably looks more like Peter Parker. Someone with that physical build lifting that much weight is <i>still</i> obviously superhuman, even if a body builder can match the feat. Though I'll admit that that aspect of things tend to be unique to the physical attributes, as the others don't leave telltale signs that can be recognized on sight. Still, someone looking at the track record of a Nova with, say, Mega-Intelligence 1 will likely note that she \u201cdidn't do the work\u201d, and is far more successful at Intelligence-related stuff than she has any right to be. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455908#post1455908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, this is a bit off topic. The House Rule I propose does nothing in any way to change how recognizable low level Mega-Attributes are, just how expensive they are to get. So, much as the topic is of interest to me as well, we should probably drop it and focus on the Polymath/Technique/Costs of Stats discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that regard, it's worth noting that several Mega-Attributes come with \u201cfree dots\u201d in appropriate Edges. I could see leveraging Technique in a similar way, with each dot in a Technique (or Polymath, of you want to keep this separate from Technique) for a Mega-Attribute giving that Mega-Attribute's rating in dots of Mega-Edges that have that Mega-Attribute as a prerequisite. <br /> <br /> But I wouldn't go beyond that. Having Mega-Might give cheap access to Mega-Intellect ought to be a straight up no-go; and I'd look askance on it providing cheap access to Mega-Dexterity or even Mega-Stamina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T04:38:39-07:00","id":1455921,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455910#post1455910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cost apart, another aspect that needs to be covered is that some of the powers many characters in comics have are covered by Mega Edges, and so they don\u2019t get covered by techniques ar all, cyberkinesis, super speed, telepathy, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely part of the idea, yeah, though certainly not all of it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455910#post1455910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your approach to the rules open this side of the rules in a way my approach don\u2019t, as you can combine super speed and shockwave to make a sonic boom, instead of 2 independent powers, but it keep powers out of the way, so a quantum attack (punch of infinite mass) and a sonic boom must be independent (bad example, because you can make sonic boom with quantum attack, but you got the idea, technique with power and mega stuff combined).</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, such things are fairly cheap in Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges (Shockwave would only take Mega-Might 1 and Shockwave to acquire, for example), which makes this not seem like a huge deal to me personally. Making it more achievable might be ideal, but can get awkward.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455910#post1455910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Another option is you can create techniques out of mega edges, instead of powers only, combining everything as you pleased. The issue there is that most of the techniques don\u2019t evolve as powers do, they just have a fixed cost and that\u2019s it (they can get tags, but it\u2019s not that many that fit) while powers can gain extra dots and tags.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I am just pointing things, not bringing solutions\u2026 maybe later I can bring something solid to discuss\u2026</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah, mix and matching Powers and Mega-Edges is tricky on a system level even if it makes sense thematically. I'm a little leery personally, and think Polymath + Techniques covers most reasonable character concepts well enough.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455918#post1455918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a quick nitpick, and then I'll drop it: the Might 5/Athletics 5 guy will look like a bodybuilder (because, frankly, he <i>is</i> a body builder); the Might 2/Athletics 0/Mega-Might 1 guy probably looks more like Peter Parker. Someone with that physical build lifting that much weight is <i>still</i> obviously superhuman, even if a body builder can match the feat. Though I'll admit that that aspect of things tend to be unique to the physical attributes, as the others don't leave telltale signs that can be recognized on sight. Still, someone looking at the track record of a Nova with, say, Mega-Intelligence 1 will likely note that she \u201cdidn't do the work\u201d, and is far more successful at Intelligence-related stuff than she has any right to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Eruption can easily change how you look, so I'm not sure this is always gonna be true, but as I said it's off topic, so I'll leave it at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455918#post1455918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that regard, it's worth noting that several Mega-Attributes come with \u201cfree dots\u201d in appropriate Edges. I could see leveraging Technique in a similar way, with each dot in a Technique (or Polymath, of you want to keep this separate from Technique) for a Mega-Attribute giving that Mega-Attribute's rating in dots of Mega-Edges that have that Mega-Attribute as a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't go beyond that. Having Mega-Might give cheap access to Mega-Intellect ought to be a straight up no-go; and I'd look askance on it providing cheap access to Mega-Dexterity or even Mega-Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's not what's happening thematically. Thematically, by taking Polymath, you're saying 'My power theme is being good at Mega-Attributes in general.' And then doing the equivalent of taking 'Techniques' of other Mega-Attributes. Hence the name. By taking it, you are saying that your character is, to some degree, a polymath, good at multiple Mega-Attributes. It's not that one actually gives you the other, one is just your 'strong suit' and takes the lead, but what's actually giving you the extra Mega-Attributes is the theme of Polymath itself. Count Orzaiz may have Mega-Manipulation as his 'strong suit' and, as a PC, would have his Polymath based on it, but that doesn't mean that his Mega-Manipulation actually gave him Mega-Stamina and Regeneration, it just means that both are thematically linked by his being a polymath, a paragon of superhuman ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","user":"Deadmanwalking","date":". 08-01-2021, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T05:16:53-07:00","id":1455925,"title":"","content":"\u201cbeing good at mega attributes in general\u201d strikes me as being too broad to be a reasonable power theme. Typically, power themes are much more specific than that. I could maybe see focusing on an arena or an approach as a reasonable power theme \u2014 someone who's really good at being forceful, or someone who's very good at mental stuff, perhaps; though even that's too broad for my liking. But everything from might to composure? That's a bit much.<br /> <br /> Power suites aren't there to give you the spirit powers on the cheap; they're there to represent someone who can use a particular power in a versatile manner. But everything that the techniques do ought to be extensions or variations of the base power.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a true polymath, pay for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T07:28:53-07:00","id":1455932,"title":"","content":"Someone mentioned this before, but some mega-attributes give free dots for regular edges. I've been thinking about house ruling this for all the mega-attributes to make them more appealing, but I'm not sure if that would make it unbalanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T07:59:51-07:00","id":1455934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455932#post1455932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone mentioned this before, but some mega-attributes give free dots for regular edges. I've been thinking about house ruling this for all the mega-attributes to make them more appealing, but I'm not sure if that would make it unbalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion is that it would unbalance a bit. The ones that give edge dots have a relatively low direct use in game, while the ones that don\u2019t are already balanced against each other is a certain way.<br /> <br /> What I may suggest to Make them appealing is to allow the character to spend Quantum points up to the MAtt rank to gain one extra dice to the pool using the attribute.<br /> For example, you have Dex 3, MDex 2 and Aim 3, if you want to attack with a gun you would roll 6 dice and reduce the complications/difficulty by 2 (MDex advantage), with no quantum cost. Using this rule you would be able to roll up to 8 dice (2 extra dice by spending 1 quantum per extra dice).<br /> <br /> Second option is to boost momentum spending, every time you use momentum and have MAtt in the used att, you gain the MAtt rank as extra dice, fir example, the same guy from before would spend a momentum to roll 3 extra dice (not spending any quantum). Notice that this extra dice is not per momentum spend, it\u2019s an one time thing, so spending 2 momentum would grant 4 dice (not 6), and 3 momentum would grant 5 dice (not 9).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T12:44:04-07:00","id":1455946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455925#post1455925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cbeing good at mega attributes in general\u201d strikes me as being too broad to be a reasonable power theme. Typically, power themes are much more specific than that. I could maybe see focusing on an arena or an approach as a reasonable power theme \u2014 someone who's really good at being forceful, or someone who's very good at mental stuff, perhaps; though even that's too broad for my liking. But everything from might to composure? That's a bit much.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A lot of existing NPCs in the setting, from Count Orzaiz, to Andy Vance, to Andre Corbin, to Ricardo Montoya-Bernal argue that it 100% is a reasonable power theme, since it's what they've got as their primary theme. Some like Divis Mal or Cestus Pax have it on top of another pretty broad power theme as well.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455925#post1455925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Power suites aren't there to give you the spirit powers on the cheap; they're there to represent someone who can use a particular power in a versatile manner. But everything that the techniques do ought to be extensions or variations of the base power.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a true polymath, pay for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I can already have 'being a polymath' for cheap by buying Boost with a Technique for Transformation (or even just either on their own). That can give me a total of something like 5s in all Attributes, plus Toughness 4 and 25 points of Mega-Attributes (as well as several points of other Powers/Mega-Edges from Transformation) on a starting character. I can already easily be a polymath without 'paying for it' any more than this, the way of doing so is just awkward, super counter to the theme of 'just being good at multiple things', and not a lot of fun if my concept doresn't involve shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> This House Rule remains inferior to that build in terms of raw number of points it provides by a fair bit, frankly. This is not actually a power up, just a less counterintuitive way to be good at multiple Mega-Attributes without breaking the bank point-wise or having to grab Powers you don't really want.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455932#post1455932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone mentioned this before, but some mega-attributes give free dots for regular edges. I've been thinking about house ruling this for all the mega-attributes to make them more appealing, but I'm not sure if that would make it unbalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It shifts the balance for most of them in a bad way, because they're fairly balanced already. The stats you'd be adding Edges to are Mega-Might, Mega-Dexterity, Mega-Stamina, and Mega-Cunning, and Mega-Resolve, and most of those already grant </span></span></span><i>really good</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> benefits. Mega-Stamina is maybe a little lower tier than many of the rest and would benefit from a boost like this, but Mega-Might and Mega-Dexterity are already absurdly good and doing this with them would, IMO, be a bad mistake, while Mega-Cunning already sort of does this (with Keen Senses). Mega-Resolve is a bit of a reflection of Mega-Composure and could maybe have a change like this, but only if you think Wound Penalties don't come up more often than emotional/social complications (since if wound penalties are more common, that makes Mega-Resolve too good comparatively).</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","user":"Deadmanwalking","date":". 08-01-2021, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T13:57:13-07:00","id":1455952,"title":"","content":"Notes that a polymath is an excellent character theme. That's a different thing than being an excellent power theme. \u201cI can do anything!\u201d isn't something that you should ever get on the cheap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T14:15:26-07:00","id":1455954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455852#post1455852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think that the problem is that Technique is too powerful: you get a whole other power for the cost of just one dot in a Mega-Edge, and the only downside is that if you want both active at once, you need to split the activation dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just remembered something easily forgotten: whenever you use a Reflexive or non-dice-pool Quantum Power as a mixed action, you pay 1 extra Quantum Point<br /> <br /> I think it's fair to use this &quot;+1 quantum point cost&quot; for <i><b>all </b></i>Techniqued Powers, not just the reflexive or non-dice-pool ones. The only power without this increased cost would be the &quot;Original Power&quot;, the one you actually bought with XP and &quot;attached&quot; the Tag initially. This may make things simpler than the current rules, and also gives a slight advantage for those novas that do not use Techniques. In fact it's almost a direct translation from 1st edition &quot;suite&quot; powers quantum cost (such as Elemental Mastery and the like).<br /> <br /> Obs: I know this tweak is probably too weak for your taste, Dataweaver; I just put it here for people that think that using a Techniqued power should be a sliiiight disadvantage during use, but don't want to go as far as you probably would. :-]<br /> <br /> I think the probable outcome of this tweak is that a nova with Techniques wouldn't feel much difference daily, but IF he encounters a nova without Techniques, he'd notice that he gets &quot;empty&quot; sooner than the other guy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T15:06:25-07:00","id":1455960,"title":"","content":"The \u201csplit dice pool\u201d thing is a rule for ALL multi action, the only difference in using more than one power from the suit is the increased cost.<br /> <br /> But honestly, the idea is you HAVE techniques to gain 2 conceptual advantages, first you get a power theme and gain anything from it, second, the costs of nova powers are too big in the long term, if you don\u2019t have it it\u2019s better to reduce the cost of \u201cnova dots\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T16:17:09-07:00","id":1455969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455952#post1455952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notes that a polymath is an excellent character theme. That's a different thing than being an excellent power theme. \u201cI can do anything!\u201d isn't something that you should ever get on the cheap.</div> </div> </div> </div>You already can get it cheap. I'm trying to make doing so less annoying, counterintuitive, and theme violating. And how is 'my powers make me better at mundane stuff' not a solid theme? Given the scope of what Quantum Powers can do, 'better at mundane actions' isn't even that broad or difficult a theme conceptually. It seems conceptually on par with 'I manipulate space and time' or 'I can control biology', which are both definitely available themes (the latter is even explicitly the basic power theme of a couple of NPCs).<br /> <br /> And many Polymath uses are actually narrower than 'better at mundane stuff', anyway. 'I'm psychic', as a theme, can easily hit north of 30 points of Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges, and in all three Approaches and both Social and Mental stats. 'I'm basically invulnerable to just about everything' is another straightforward theme that can easily go north of 30 points, and spans Mental, Physical, and Social (if 'everything' includes things like intimidation). There are dozens more such themes, and they vary enough that making people try and justify them each individually is rather pointless.<br /> <br /> But I don't think the guy whose theme is 'I'm psychic' or 'I'm basically invulnerable' should be either penalized as compared to the one whose theme is 'I control gravity' or 'I manipulate space and time' or forced to take weird and counter-thematic powers to achieve what they're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","user":"Deadmanwalking","date":". 08-01-2021, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T17:05:53-07:00","id":1455973,"title":"","content":"I like your take on the problem Deadmanwalking, but I'm not entirely satisfied with the end result. I like that it's similar to Technique; I don't like that it enables things as Mega-Composure enhancing Mega-Strenght, and last but not least, I don't like that you put Mega-Edges inside it. I think these should be completely separate: one solution to have Mega-Attributes with costs similar to Techniques, and OTHER solution to make you use Mega-Edges that &quot;you don't have&quot; (but my gut tells me that Maxing Out is enough to solve the 2nd problem). Also, since the &quot;Techniqued&quot; Mega-Attributes also count as pre-requisites, the char can simply buy the Mega-Edges he wants.<br /> <br /> I'll think about it, and if I get to a solid solution, I may post it here; for now I'm inclined to use something in your lines but without touching Mega-Edges. Also, I'm almost decided to use the &quot;+1quantum point to every technique&quot; tweak that I spoke before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","user":"Timecrafter","date":". 08-01-2021, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T17:25:27-07:00","id":1455977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455973#post1455973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your take on the problem Deadmanwalking, but I'm not entirely satisfied with the end result. I like that it's similar to Technique; I don't like that it enables things as Mega-Composure enhancing Mega-Strenght, and last but not least, I don't like that you put Mega-Edges inside it. I think these should be completely separate: one solution to have Mega-Attributes with costs similar to Techniques, and OTHER solution to make you use Mega-Edges that &quot;you don't have&quot; (but my gut tells me that Maxing Out is enough to solve the 2nd problem). Also, since the &quot;Techniqued&quot; Mega-Attributes also count as pre-requisites, the char can simply buy the Mega-Edges he wants.<br /> <br /> I'll think about it, and if I get to a solid solution, I may post it here; for now I'm inclined to use something in your lines but without touching Mega-Edges. Also, I'm almost decided to use the &quot;+1quantum point to every technique&quot; tweak that I spoke before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the 'Composure increasing Might' thing is just a perspective issue. That's not really what's happening. If your theme doesn't involve Mega-Might, then raising Mega-Composure doesn't raise it, if your theme does involve Mega-Might, then raising Mega-Composure (if it's your highest Mega-Attribute) represents more than just raising Mega-Composure it represents raising your whole theme, which may coincidentally also raise Mega-Might. <br /> <br /> Say your theme is 'Wuxia-style mystical martial arts', for example, suddenly increasing your 'enlightenment' (ie: Mega-Composure) increasing your physical prowess makes perfect sense, because it's appropriate to the theme, and that's just one example. As another example, if your theme is 'transhuman perfection' and your highest Mega-Attribute is Mega-Intellect and you raise it, it's not getting smarter that increases your Mega-Might as well, it's getting closer to that ideal of transhuman perfection you are epitomizing, Intellect is just the most obvious way in which you epitomize that ideal.<br /> <br /> As for Mega-Edges, you sort of need them rolled in or the whole thing doesn't work nearly as well for the vast majority of concepts. Andy Vance needs Toughness to work properly, for example, while the 'psychic' example I mention above needs a lot of different Mega-Edges to work. Really, if you want something more limited, you'd probably need to do it broken down by something like Physical/Social/Mental but still having Mega-Edges available than trying to separate Mega-Edges and Mega-Attributes from each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T22:34:54-07:00","id":1455993,"title":"","content":"Being Super-<i>Human </i>seems like a perfectly valid power theme to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T23:05:41-07:00","id":1455994,"title":"","content":"this theme is named &quot;Paragon&quot;, at Aberrant core book p.291 :-]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T23:32:25-07:00","id":1455995,"title":"","content":"If going by themes in the Appendix, 'Fighter', 'Thinker', 'Paragon', 'Performer', and 'Tank' all, by default, have absolutely no Quantum Powers and yet maintain coherent themes that would strongly benefit from the use of Polymath, though yes, Paragon is the most direct example of a power theme of 'better than other people at mundane stuff' (though the others all have that as well, just in a specific arena).<br /> <br /> Indeed, the issue Polymath is designed to solve can be summed up by the fact that the 'Shapeshifter' Morph option in that Appendix is a better tank than the actual 'Tank' option by a fair bit (and can be made even more superior easily by making Transformation Maintained and giving it another level of Extra Traits), and the Elemental is at least as good and both have a lot of other stuff they can do as well, while the Tank is much more of a one trick pony. That disparity is the thing I'm trying to fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T03:02:28-07:00","id":1455998,"title":"","content":"Again, perfectly valid <i>character</i> themes. <i>Power</i> themes, not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T03:21:24-07:00","id":1455999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455998#post1455998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, perfectly valid <i>character</i> themes. <i>Power</i> themes, not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly disagree. A power theme is anything that can be briefly described as a single clear thematic statement 'I'm better than normal people at stuff' is a single clear thematic statement, as is 'I'm basically a Wuxia protagonist' or 'I effectively have psychic powers' or 'I'm a speedster, like the Flash' or 'I'm a feral monster, more beast than man' (all of which can be done entirely with Polymath). None of those are broader than 'control of biology' or other broad power sets, and several are actually narrower.<br /> <br /> A character can have multiple power themes, it's true (Divis Mal, for example, has both 'I'm superhumanly competent in every area' and 'I create and control plasma'), but 'I'm beyond human at mundane actions' is not notably broader or weirder than 'I have absolute control of my own density' or 'I channel the powers of various totem animals' both of which are valid as single power themes, and most Polymath uses are actually narrower than being good at everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","user":"Deadmanwalking","date":". 08-02-2021, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T06:53:18-07:00","id":1456005,"title":"","content":"A couple of thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) The main difference between a baseline using might Scale through skill tricks or whatever and a nova using Mega-Might is the nova doesn't need to worry about things like leverage or structural integrity of the object they're lifting. So, a nova can grab the bumper of a car and swing the whole thing around without worrying about the bumper ripping off. An professional weight lifter can't do that.<br /> <br /> 2) That Polymath mega-edge is going to make being a speedster very cheap compared to what it is now. I'm going to guess probably too cheap, but I haven't run the numbers. Honestly, the fact it gives mega-edge dots makes it WAY more powerful than Technique giving another power, IMO.<br /> <br /> 3) I think the thing which balances buying Boost vs. buying Mega-Attributes is Boost doesn't give you Mega-Edges. Mega-Attributes are nice, but they are kind of narrow in application. (Except maybe Mega-Might.) You really need to dive into Mega-Edges to get the most out of your Mega-Attributes, and Boost doesn't let you do that. Use Boost all you want, it'll never make you a speedster or able to manipulate masses of people over a vid feed..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T08:19:20-07:00","id":1456010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1455850#post1455850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use a similar idea, but just giving more options to Technique Mega Edge (but making one for it is a better option).<br /> <br /> In my idea you add the technique to a Mega Attribute and gain the <b>MAtt rank times the technique mega edge dots</b> as dots of Mega Edges related to that MAtt (Technique is not a valid one).<br /> <br /> So if you get Technique to Mega Might, you can get Mega Lifting, Mega Crush, etc, but not any Mega Cunning mega edge for example, or any dot in Mega Dexterity.<br /> <br /> A bit less versatile than yours, but I honestly prefer that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if you have MAtt 2 associated with Technique 3 you get 6 dots of Mega edges?<br /> <br /> I assume that for Mega Edges that dont relate to a Mega Attribute you follow a &quot;if the player can justify it&quot; rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T09:42:21-07:00","id":1456012,"title":"","content":"I agree with Florin about Mega-Edges. I can see Techniques for Mega-Attributes being something fair if the numbers are well thought, but not if they give Mega-Edges too. I really think these are 2 different problems; for now, I'm leaning towards this:<br /> <br /> 1st) Create a Mega-Edge that is essentially &quot;Technique for Mega-Attributes&quot;. You get one Mega as the basis, you gain other Megas, but NOT Mega-Edges.<br /> <br /> 2nd) Create <i>another </i>Mega-Edge that is essentially &quot;Technique for Mega-Edges&quot;. You choose one Mega Edge as the basis (superspeed is the first to come to my mind mind), you gain other Mega-Edges thematically linked as Techniques, but NOT Mega-Attribute dots.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T12:00:32-07:00","id":1456022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456010#post1456010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if you have MAtt 2 associated with Technique 3 you get 6 dots of Mega edges?<br /> <br /> I assume that for Mega Edges that dont relate to a Mega Attribute you follow a &quot;if the player can justify it&quot; rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>Double yes\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T12:10:23-07:00","id":1456023,"title":"","content":"On the Boost comment, Boost really make the Nova super Human, with emphasis on human. The nova don\u2019t get most of the reality bending side of being a Nova, just a big wow on the scale of what can be done by a human.<br /> <br /> Now, on the speedster comment, I am quite sure a speedster is one of the most expensive builds of the \u201cstandard super team\u201d, so I think it\u2019s not that bad. You end up with a very good speedster in the char gen, not the flash, but maybe a MCU Quicksilver with a solid speed and flexibility.<br /> <br /> And finally, Mega Might is the only MAtt that stand out by itself, and that\u2019s why I think it\u2019s not intended to cause scale damage straight from its rank with a punch. But nobody likes the idea\u2026 ok\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T12:22:52-07:00","id":1456025,"title":"","content":"I ran the math (pun intended?) on a speedster. With no transformations or transcendence, you can get Q5, MDex 5, MMight 5, Defense 1, Mega-Speed, Rapid Strike, Toughness 2. You may not get the MCunning initiative boost, but if anyone in your group has it, you might be able to convince them to let you take the first spot in the order. Then, you attack with a 5 point reduction to complications and difficulty to hit, hit at Scale 6, and can spend a quantum to add 5 enhancement. You also add 6 dice to your Defense roll and have 2 dots of Toughness. Hard to hit, has a hard time missing, and hits really hard. Oh, and they run at supersonic speeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T12:32:39-07:00","id":1456028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456025#post1456025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran the math (pun intended?) on a speedster. With no transformations or transcendence, you can get Q5, MDex 5, MMight 5, Defense 1, Mega-Speed, Rapid Strike, Toughness 2. You may not get the MCunning initiative boost, but if anyone in your group has it, you might be able to convince them to let you take the first spot in the order. Then, you attack with a 5 point reduction to complications and difficulty to hit, hit at Scale 6, and can spend a quantum to add 5 enhancement. You also add 6 dice to your Defense roll and have 2 dots of Toughness. Hard to hit, has a hard time missing, and hits really hard. Oh, and they run at supersonic speeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, running at super sonic speeds is a good extra for this set of powers\u2026<br /> <br /> Honestly Mega Might 5 should not be part of the pack. You mean MDex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T12:44:03-07:00","id":1456029,"title":"","content":"MDex is already in there. MMight is because force equals mass times acceleration. If you increase the acceleration enough, and you can apply a whole lot of force. Heck, put a Restriction on MMight so it only applies to power Scale and not might Scale. Then you get even more dots to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T13:06:13-07:00","id":1456030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456005#post1456005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) The main difference between a baseline using might Scale through skill tricks or whatever and a nova using Mega-Might is the nova doesn't need to worry about things like leverage or structural integrity of the object they're lifting. So, a nova can grab the bumper of a car and swing the whole thing around without worrying about the bumper ripping off. An professional weight lifter can't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is true, but usually not obvious at Scale 2 (since that's not even close to enough to lift a car). Mega-Might 1 is definitely unnatural, I'm just saying it's usually a subtle sort of unnatural.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456005#post1456005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) That Polymath mega-edge is going to make being a speedster very cheap compared to what it is now. I'm going to guess probably too cheap, but I haven't run the numbers. Honestly, the fact it gives mega-edge dots makes it WAY more powerful than Technique giving another power, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speedster isn't any more powerful than many Quantum Power based builds, IMO, just more expensive, so I consider this a perk.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that you can pretty readily get a couple of points of strategic Mega-Edges with Q-Tech pretty readily. That has its own limitations, but is a worthwhile thing to note as available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456005#post1456005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I think the thing which balances buying Boost vs. buying Mega-Attributes is Boost doesn't give you Mega-Edges. Mega-Attributes are nice, but they are kind of narrow in application. (Except maybe Mega-Might.) You really need to dive into Mega-Edges to get the most out of your Mega-Attributes, and Boost doesn't let you do that. Use Boost all you want, it'll never make you a speedster or able to manipulate masses of people over a vid feed..</div> </div> </div> </div>In direct conflict, though, the Boost user will win something like 90% of the direct conflicts they come into with the Polymath (everything outside the Polymath's specialty) because, on top of the Mega-Attributes all their normal Attributes are at 5. That's not a small comparative advantage (indeed, in xp terms, it's something like 200 xp worth of stats on a starting character) for the Boost/Transformation character I suggest in the first post that's on top of the 36 points of Mega-Attributes/Mega-Edges/Powers they can bring to bear, for effectively 632 xp of stuff. Polymath makes for, at roughly the same cost, only 240 xp worth of stuff (20 dots of Mega-attributes and Edges at Quantum 4, Mega-Attribute 4, Polymath 4). Mega-Edges are certainly good, but they're not good enough to compensate for that disparity. Even at Quantum 5 with maximal investment, Polymath maxes out at 360 xp worth of traits (for a cost of 120 xp, plus Quantum costs), while a 120 xp investment in Boost/Transformation can easily hit 50 dots of Mega-Attributes/Edges/Powers (25 from Boost 5, 25 from Transformation with Extra Traits), plus the 200 xp of mundane Attributes and thus 800 xp of stuff or thereabouts.<br /> <br /> Polymath gives a good, sizeable, discount, but it's nowhere close to the best you can get point for point, so you're already paying a premium for comprehensive Mega-Edge access in many ways.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456012#post1456012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Florin about Mega-Edges. I can see Techniques for Mega-Attributes being something fair if the numbers are well thought, but not if they give Mega-Edges too. I really think these are 2 different problems; for now, I'm leaning towards this:</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456012#post1456012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1st) Create a Mega-Edge that is essentially &quot;Technique for Mega-Attributes&quot;. You get one Mega as the basis, you gain other Megas, but NOT Mega-Edges.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">2nd) Create <i>another </i>Mega-Edge that is essentially &quot;Technique for Mega-Edges&quot;. You choose one Mega Edge as the basis (superspeed is the first to come to my mind mind), you gain other Mega-Edges thematically linked as Techniques, but NOT Mega-Attribute dots.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The difficulty is that Mega-Edges are almost always only 1 dot (occasionally 2), with only very occasional exceptions, making Technique not work super well for them in most cases (for example, adding this as an option to Mega Speed does quite literally nothing...it's a 1 dot Edge, so buying other Edges off it with a Polymath equivalent saves 0 xp over just buying them). It would work if you based it on a Mega-Attribute to get only Mega-Edges, but that differs from Polymath only semantically in most ways.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456025#post1456025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran the math (pun intended?) on a speedster. With no transformations or transcendence, you can get Q5, MDex 5, MMight 5, Defense 1, Mega-Speed, Rapid Strike, Toughness 2. You may not get the MCunning initiative boost, but if anyone in your group has it, you might be able to convince them to let you take the first spot in the order. Then, you attack with a 5 point reduction to complications and difficulty to hit, hit at Scale 6, and can spend a quantum to add 5 enhancement. You also add 6 dice to your Defense roll and have 2 dots of Toughness. Hard to hit, has a hard time missing, and hits really hard. Oh, and they run at supersonic speeds.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sure, if you have Stm 1 (since you need normal Might and Dex 5 for this and that necessitates starting Stm 1 on a starting character investing like this). So this example is a tad more extreme than most characters are gonna be, at least to start with.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That said, looking at the build for what it is, it's quite good, as attacks go, but a Quantum 5 Boost/Transformation guy can easily have Mega-Might 5, Mega-Dex 5, Toughness 5, and Piercing Claws, a combination that is probably superior in a fight (and certainly on par), and has better utility as well since shapeshifting is generally gonna be better than moving fast as far as problem solving tools go. That guy also has at least 1 or 2 in every other Mega-Attribute and straight 5s in the mundane ones, plus Mega-Sensory stuff and other Body Modifications at need while the speedster is a one trick pony in a lot of ways.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Which is all to say that Polymath is intentionally good, but it's not better than existing options, which was my goal. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","user":"Deadmanwalking","date":". 08-02-2021, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T13:32:52-07:00","id":1456031,"title":"","content":"I'd be curious to see how the fact the Boost character is going to be burning through a lot of quantum points if they need to change forms or keep Transformation up for very long would hamper them in a day where they have more than one fight. The speedster can go all day long, only burning quantum points for their Rapid Strike, whereas the booster/transformer doesn't recover any quantum points as long as they are boosted and/or transformed, and their powers are pretty quantum point-intensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T13:33:27-07:00","id":1456032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456030#post1456030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The difficulty is that Mega-Edges are almost always only 1 dot (occasionally 2), with only very occasional exceptions, making Technique not work super well for them in most cases (for example, adding this as an option to Mega Speed does quite literally nothing...it's a 1 dot Edge, so buying other Edges off it with a Polymath equivalent saves 0 xp over just buying them). It would work if you based it on a Mega-Attribute to get only Mega-Edges, but that differs from Polymath only semantically in most ways.</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) I see your point, but your solution still seems overpowered. Remember that you are comparing it to an exploit (&quot;permanent&quot; Boost). I think it could be fair if you state that the Techniqued &quot;ghost dots&quot; you gain can be used to buy Mega-Attributes OR Mega-Edges related to the character Theme. So, John would use his 3 &quot;techniqued&quot; points to buy Mega-Strenght 3, but Mary would rather use them to get Mega-Strenght 2 + Quantum Leap (1).<br /> <br /> PS: Unrelated - don't you all think Quantum Leap prerequisite should be Mega-Might ONE, and not two? I really think 2 is a mistake there. XD<br /> <br /> 2) I don't like the name Polymath, because, for me, Polymath is more about Skills than Attributes (so I'd use another name). \ud83d\ude05 Heck, this opens another can of worms: what about &quot;Technique&quot; to Skills??? Would it work? Why/why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T14:10:59-07:00","id":1456034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456031#post1456031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be curious to see how the fact the Boost character is going to be burning through a lot of quantum points if they need to change forms or keep Transformation up for very long would hamper them in a day where they have more than one fight. The speedster can go all day long, only burning quantum points for their Rapid Strike, whereas the booster/transformer doesn't recover any quantum points as long as they are boosted and/or transformed, and their powers are pretty quantum point-intensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the theoretical character has both at Maintained, so they just activate them when they wake up in the morning and then have them on all day (barring getting knocked out), with no further expenditure (and can shift around the Transformation dots whenever they like outside combat). In the long run they probably grab Absorption of some sort with Siphon or Quantum Leech and use that to refill Quantum as necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456032#post1456032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1) I see your point, but your solution still seems overpowered. Remember that you are comparing it to an exploit (&quot;permanent&quot; Boost). I think it could be fair if you state that the Techniqued &quot;ghost dots&quot; you gain can be used to buy Mega-Attributes OR Mega-Edges related to the character Theme. So, John would use his 3 &quot;techniqued&quot; points to buy Mega-Strenght 3, but Mary would rather use them to get Mega-Strenght 2 + Quantum Leap (1).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Er...that's already how it works, I think? The dots from Polymath don't double up, you have one pool of points to distribute among Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges, every dot you get in one is one you don't get in the other.<br /> <br /> For example, John has Mega-Stamina 3 and Polymath (Mega-Stamina) 3, so he has 9 points to play with from Polymath. He uses them to buy Mega-Might 3 (3 points), Toughness 3 with Impervious (4 points), Adaptation (1 point), and Regeneration (1 point). He is now out of points. Alice could get the same distribution but with Quantum Leap but would need to drop Mega-Might to 2 or lose Adaptation (or something else) to do so. This is just how Polymath works and is intended to work, and I thought my wording conveyed that?<br /> <br /> Or am I just completely misunderstanding what you're saying?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456032#post1456032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">PS: Unrelated - don't you all think Quantum Leap prerequisite should be Mega-Might ONE, and not two? I really think 2 is a mistake there. XD</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Probably. I'd be inclined to let someone take it at Mega-Might 1, anyway.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456032#post1456032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">2) I don't like the name Polymath, because, for me, Polymath is more about Skills than Attributes (so I'd use another name). \ud83d\ude05 Heck, this opens another can of worms: what about &quot;Technique&quot; to Skills??? Would it work? Why/why not?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The name was pretty arbitrary, being the first thing I came up with that was appropriate. I'd change it if I could come up with a better one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And Skills are already sorta handled by Instant Expert, though I'm a little unsure how that works (specifically, does Mega-Intellect Scale apply? I'm unsure. Also, can it only ever be used once per task type?)</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","user":"Deadmanwalking","date":". 08-02-2021, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T20:59:20-07:00","id":1456051,"title":"","content":"Re-reading, I could see how the Polymath description might be confusing. Here's a slight rewording clarifying my intent in regards to how it works:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Polymath (O \u2013 OOOOO):</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Prerequisites:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Quantum equal to dots, one Mega-Attribute at 2+</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Select one Mega-Attribute. For every dot they take in this Mega-Edge the Nova receives additional dots in a combination of Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges equal to that Mega-Attribute's rating. These points may not be used to purchase the Technique or Q-Tech Mega-Edges or to increase any Mega-Attribute or Mega-Edge above the rating of the original Mega-Attribute. A character may only ever have this Edge once, though if another Mega-Attribute ever equals their rating in the Mega-Attribute it effects, they may switch it to be based on that Mega-Attribute instead. Since this Mega-Edge has no mechanical effect beyond changing costs, it should not generally be listed on NPCs.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T23:24:41-07:00","id":1456054,"title":"","content":"aaaah, I got it now. it was really about the wording. \ud83d\ude05<br /> <br /> I'd say something more like &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\">Select one Mega-Attribute. For every dot they take in this Mega-Edge, the Nova receives a number of points equal to that Mega-Attribute's rating to form a special pool. U</span>sing a 1:1 ratio, this special pool must be spent to purchase any <i>other </i>Mega-Attributes, or any Mega-Edges, or any Tags related to <i>another</i> Mega-Attribute or to a Mega-Edge (but <i>not </i>Tags for Quantum Powers). Beware: the Nova still has to posses any needed prerequisites (but nothing precludes them to use the pool to buy those), and once chosen, all choices are permanent (just like they are when you pay experience points).&quot;<br /> <br /> Writing rules with good wording is very difficult, you can probably get some idea from mine to make it better. \ud83d\ude05<br /> <br /> If I have an idea about a new name, I'll write it here later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (Also, it still needs a little descriptive text, such as the example of &quot;Mind Peace&quot; (a.k.a. Mega-Resolve) enhancing Dexterity and the like, so the player knows he has to &quot;follow a theme that makes sense&quot;).<br /> <br /> PS: any Idea why Technique goes up to 5 only? Other Mega-Edges go all the way to 9. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","user":"Timecrafter","date":". 08-03-2021, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T00:11:08-07:00","id":1456055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456054#post1456054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">aaaah, I got it now. it was really about the wording. \ud83d\ude05<br /> <br /> I'd say something more like &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\">Select one Mega-Attribute. For every dot they take in this Mega-Edge, the Nova receives a number of points equal to that Mega-Attribute's rating to form a special pool. U</span>sing a 1:1 ratio, this special pool must be spent to purchase any <i>other </i>Mega-Attributes, or any Mega-Edges, or any Tags related to <i>another</i> Mega-Attribute or to a Mega-Edge (but <i>not </i>Tags for Quantum Powers). Beware: the Nova still has to posses any needed prerequisites (but nothing precludes them to use the pool to buy those), and once chosen, all choices are permanent (just like they are when you pay experience points).&quot;<br /> <br /> Writing rules with good wording is very difficult, you can probably get some idea from mine to make it better. \ud83d\ude05</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I <i>think</i> my new wording works okay, but yeah precise enough wording can be tricky. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456054#post1456054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have an idea about a new name, I'll write it here later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (Also, it still needs a little descriptive text, such as the example of &quot;Mind Peace&quot; (a.k.a. Mega-Resolve) enhancing Dexterity and the like, so the player knows he has to &quot;follow a theme that makes sense&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think there are plenty of themes that allow basically any purchase, which makes such a specific note a little unnecessary in many ways, but I'd add flavor text if I was making an unofficial supplement or something, yeah. Given it's just a House Rule for personal use (and the use of others who might be interested), I'll likely skip it.<br /> <br /> I mean, theme is relative, so any example can be misconstrued. Mega-Resolve might easily be the core Mega-Attribute for someone whose concept is 'transcending all limits through sheer will', and that guy is 100% grabbing Mega-Physical stuff for some of their Polymath points. I'd also definitely consider it if building Captain America using Polymath in this system (it's that or Mega-Composure...I think I eventually decided on Mega-Composure, but it was a near thing). Even a seemingly obvious note that you can't get too heavily into Mega-Physicals if your theme is 'psychic powers' is not as clear cut as it looks at first glance (a 'precognitive' might well have some serious Mega-Dexterity, for example). I could maybe do something, but I'd have to be really careful.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456054#post1456054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS: any Idea why Technique goes up to 5 only? Other Mega-Edges go all the way to 9. \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I've decided to interpret it as an intentional limit on how much of a cost reducer Technique is allowed to be. It's allowed to multiply your investment in a Power to a total of 6 times its original cost, but no more. Just piling on an unlimited number of Technique equivalents is one easy way to break Mutants and Masterminds, so this seems plausible. That's one reason why I kept that limitation for Polymath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T05:38:43-07:00","id":1456068,"title":"","content":"I think I found a new name: &quot;Well-Rounded&quot;!<br /> <br /> PS: I was thinking, there should be a Powered Edge to be the &quot;Technique&quot; for Skills (this one I would call <i>Polymath</i>). if you think about it, there are &quot;superheroes&quot; or &quot;superhumans&quot; that are very broadly competent... but it's really perfect for <i>Talents</i>. I don't remember if the Core has something like this, but it's a fairly common trope that the &quot;Scientist&quot; of movies knows about practically all science areas, plus engineering, plus medicine. And that uber-compent guys have high levels in &quot;all&quot; abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","user":"Timecrafter","date":". 08-03-2021, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T23:42:30-07:00","id":1456104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456068#post1456068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I found a new name: &quot;Well-Rounded&quot;!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I prefer single words personally, and Polymath and Well-Rounded are basically synonyms, so I'm not convinced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455849-a-technique-equivalent-for-mega-attributes?p=1456068#post1456068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS: I was thinking, there should be a Powered Edge to be the &quot;Technique&quot; for Skills (this one I would call <i>Polymath</i>). if you think about it, there are &quot;superheroes&quot; or &quot;superhumans&quot; that are very broadly competent... but it's really perfect for <i>Talents</i>. I don't remember if the Core has something like this, but it's a fairly common trope that the &quot;Scientist&quot; of movies knows about practically all science areas, plus engineering, plus medicine. And that uber-compent guys have high levels in &quot;all&quot; abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a lot less confident inventing Gifts than something like Polymath in terms of power level issues so I'm unsure on specific mechanics, but I agree that this is thematically on point for Talents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T02:26:39-07:00","id":1456112,"title":"","content":"I don't see them as perfect synonyms, look:<br /> <br /> Polymath - keywords: learning, knowledge, study (so I think &quot;Skills&quot;).<br /> <a href=\"https://www.thefreedictionary.com/polymath\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.thefreedictionary.com/polymath</a><br /> <br /> Well-Rounded - keywords: developed, well-balanced, fully developed, many-sided -- (so I think &quot;Attributes&quot;).<br /> <a href=\"https://www.thefreedictionary.com/well+rounded\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.thefreedictionary.com/well+rounded</a><br /> <br /> a one-word synonym to &quot;Well-Rounded&quot; is &quot;Comprehensive&quot;; sadly it could be confused with &quot;Comprehensible&quot; (that has a completely unrelated meaning). :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}